{"uid":"e097ec52d5f99dfa","name":"test_huge_output_line_does_not_kill_job","fullName":"tests.test_e2e#test_huge_output_line_does_not_kill_job","historyId":"8c7a77dd381f0848aba2aae46f56afd2","time":{"start":1791930837503,"stop":1791930840496,"duration":2993},"description":"pi emits full message snapshots per NDJSON event; a single line can be\n    hundreds of KiB. Regression: this used to raise 'Separator is not found'\n    and fail the entire job instead of at most one iteration.\n\n    Task 002 (A.6, #216/#217): this body makes exactly one `engine_factory()`\n    call, so exactly one engine starts over the run dir it uses -- there is\n    no second, overlapping engine here to name. `tests/conftest.py`'s\n    `LiveRun` derives the registry-less run dir from `tmp_path` alone, not\n    from `run_id` (`self.run_dir = tmp / \"run\"`), so every `LiveRun` this\n    ONE test's body constructs would land on the same path -- that is the\n    latent collision this class of test can hit, but only across multiple\n    `engine_factory()` calls inside one test body, which this test does not\n    make. No barrier is added here: there is nothing to serialize against.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>pi emits full message snapshots per NDJSON event; a single line can be<br />\nhundreds of KiB. Regression: this used to raise 'Separator is not found'<br />\nand fail the entire job instead of at most one iteration.</p>\n<pre><code>Task 002 (A.6, #216/#217): this body makes exactly one `engine_factory()`\ncall, so exactly one engine starts over the run dir it uses -- there is\nno second, overlapping engine here to name. `tests/conftest.py`'s\n`LiveRun` derives the registry-less run dir from `tmp_path` alone, not\nfrom `run_id` (`self.run_dir = tmp / &quot;run&quot;`), so every `LiveRun` this\nONE test's body constructs would land on the same path -- that is the\nlatent collision this class of test can hit, but only across multiple\n`engine_factory()` calls inside one test body, which this t